  "id": "COMPOUND:14884 - PROTEIN:4923",
  "verbalization": "Borapetoside D is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Borapetoside D directly targets SF-188, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (2R,10S,12R,16R,18R)-6,7-dihydroxy-8-(hydroxymethyl)-4,18-dimethyl-14-nonyl-16-prop-1-en-2-yl-9,13,15,19-tetraoxahexacyclo[12.4.1.01,11.02,6.08,10.012,16]nonadec-3-en-5-one and (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one. These latter compounds are both targets of Neuropilin-2, indicating a potential mechanism by which Borapetoside D may influence Neuropilin-2 through the activation of these downstream pathways. The integration of these findings suggests that Borapetoside D may exert its biological effects by modulating the activity of SF-188, which in turn affects Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence supports a pathway where Borapetoside D acts as a modulator of a complex network of targets, ultimately influencing Neuropilin-2.",
